{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["Who dwell in Se'ir — these are not those Edom who came out with sword to meet Israel, for about them it is written: כאשר עשו לי בני עשו היושבים בשעיר, but Edom sold them nothing at all, for it is written about them: ויט ישראל מעליו. This is the interpretation of Rabbenu. But to me, the younger, his words do not seem correct in this matter. For the children of Esav who dwell in Se'ir are Edom, for we find no settlement of theirs except on Mount Se'ir, and their name is mentioned in its place in every reading. And what is difficult for Rabbenu — כאשר עשו לי בני עשו — is not a refutation, for it refers only to what is written above: אוכל בכסף תשבירני — כאשר עשו לי בני עשו: that we took nothing from them except by purchase, as stated in the matter: אתם עוברים בגבול אחיכם בני עשו וגו׳ אבל אוכל תכרו מאתם בכסף ואכלתם. וגם מים תכרו מאתם בכסף ושתיתם. וכן עשיתם כמו שצוה הקב״ה, כמו שנאמר: כאשר עשו לי בני עשו — in the manner of their journey toward Mount Se'ir, Moshe sent to the king of Edom to let them pass through his land to the land of Israel. And to this thing he did not listen to them, for he did not want them all to enter his land together, lest they destroy the land, and therefore: ויצא אדום לקראתו בעם כבד וביד חזקה, and therefore: ויט ישראל מעליו. But in any case they would purchase from them along their route whatever they needed, and this is the truth and the straight." "And they will fear you — from the pattern of וְיֵשְׁבוּ and וְיֵדְעוּ and וְיֹאמְרוּ, but וְיָרְאוּ את ה׳, וידעו כי שמי ה׳ — from the pattern of וְאָמְרוּ and וְהָלְכוּ, and all of them are in the future tense."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "I read קִרִיָה as 'reading' (i.e., scriptural passage). The phrase ולדבר הזה לא שמע אליהם is rendered with the king of Edom as implied subject."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:20.382313900Z", :tra